PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L10U1.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":10,"cefr":"B2+","unit":1,"theme":"Learning for Tomorrow","essential_question":"What will students need to learn to succeed in a changing world?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1","title":"Never Before Had Schools Faced Such a Challenge: Inversion After Negative Adverbials","objectives":["Students will be able to use inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials for formal emphasis.","Students will be able to add do, does or did when the sentence has no auxiliary verb.","I can write \"Never before had schools faced such a challenge.\"","I can write \"Not only did teachers learn new technology, but they also changed how they taught.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام التقديم والتأخير بعد الظروف المنفية والمقيِّدة للتوكيد الرسمي.","سيتمكن الطلاب من إضافة do أو does أو did عندما لا يوجد فعل مساعد في الجملة.","أستطيع أن أكتب Never before had schools faced such a challenge.","أستطيع أن أكتب Not only did teachers learn new technology, but they also changed how they taught."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"curriculum","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kɚˈɪkjələm/","definition":"all the subjects and content taught in a school or course","arabic":"المنهج الدراسي","example":"The new curriculum includes coding from Grade 4.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS1-W01"},{"word":"platform","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈplætˌfɔrm/","definition":"a digital system or website used for a particular purpose","arabic":"منصة","example":"Students submit their homework on an online platform.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS1-W02"},{"word":"thrive","pos":"verb","ipa":"/θraɪv/","definition":"to grow, develop or be successful","arabic":"يزدهر / ينجح","example":"Some students thrive in online classes.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS1-W03"},{"word":"lifelong learning","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˈlaɪˈflɔŋ ˈlɝnɪŋ/","definition":"continuing to learn throughout your life","arabic":"التعلّم مدى الحياة","example":"Lifelong learning helps people adapt to new jobs.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"In formal English, when a negative or restrictive adverbial comes at the start of a sentence for emphasis, the word order changes to question order: adverbial + auxiliary + subject + main verb. Normal: Schools had never faced such a challenge. Inverted: Never before had schools faced such a challenge.\nCommon adverbials: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Little, Nowhere, At no time, Under no circumstances, On no account. Two-part patterns: Not only + aux + subject…, but (subject) also…; Hardly / Scarcely + had + subject + past participle + when…; No sooner + had + subject + past participle + than….\nIf there is no auxiliary (present or past simple), add do / does / did: Teachers rarely agree. → Rarely do teachers agree. Anyone little knew… → Little did anyone know… Only the first clause is inverted: Hardly had we started when the alarm rang. (NOT (not: when did the alarm ring))\nNegative adverbial + auxiliary + subject + verb\nno auxiliary → do / does / did + subject + base verb\nHardly / Scarcely… when • No sooner… than • Not only…, but also\ninvert only the clause that begins with the adverbial","examples":["Never have I met such a patient teacher.","Rarely do students enjoy exams.","Not only did she pass the course, but she also won a scholarship.","Hardly had the lesson begun when the power went off.","No sooner had the bell rung than everyone rushed out.","Under no circumstances should students share their passwords.","Little did he know that he would become a professor one day.","Nowhere is critical thinking more important than in science."],"common_errors":["✗ Never I have seen such a beautiful school. → ✓ Never have I seen such a beautiful school. (Inversion: auxiliary before the subject.)","✗ Rarely students enjoy exams. → ✓ Rarely do students enjoy exams. (No auxiliary → add do.)","✗ No sooner had the bell rung when everyone left. → ✓ No sooner had the bell rung than everyone left. (No sooner… than.)","✗ Hardly had we started when did the alarm ring. → ✓ Hardly had we started when the alarm rang. (Invert only the first clause.)"],"arabic":"عندما يأتي ظرف منفي أو مقيِّد في أول الجملة للتوكيد، يتغيّر ترتيب الكلمات إلى ترتيب السؤال: الظرف + الفعل المساعد + الفاعل + الفعل الرئيس: Never before had schools faced such a challenge.\nالظروف الشائعة: Never وRarely وSeldom وLittle وNowhere وUnder no circumstances، والأنماط: Not only… but also، Hardly… when، No sooner… than.\nإذا لم يوجد فعل مساعد نضيف do / does / did: Rarely do students enjoy exams.\nنقلب ترتيب الجملة الأولى فقط، وهذا أسلوب رسمي يُستخدم في الخطب والمقالات."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Never Before Had Schools Faced Such a Challenge: Inversion After Negative Adverbials”. Let’s learn inversion (auxiliary + subject + verb) after negative and restrictive adverbials at the start of a sentence: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Not only… but also, Hardly / Scarcely… when, No sooner… than, Under no circumstances / On no account / At no time, Little, Nowhere; adding do/does/did when there is no auxiliary together.","on_screen":"GV-L10-U1-LS1 | Never Before Had Schools Faced Such a Challenge: Inversion After Negative Adverbials","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Learning Without Walls”: Never before had Saudi schools faced a challenge like the one in March 2020. Hardly had students settled into the new term when classrooms across the Kingdom closed because of the pandemic. Within weeks, millions of students were learning online through a national platform called Madrasati. Not only did teachers have to learn new technology, but they also had to rethink the way they taught. Seldom had so many people changed their habits so quickly. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Never before had Saudi schools faced a challenge like the one in March 2020. Hardly had students settled into the new term when classrooms across the Kingdom closed because of the pandemic. Within weeks, millions of students were learning online through a national platform called Madrasati. Not only did teachers have to learn new technology, but they also had to rethink the way they taught. Seldom had so many people changed their habits so quickly.","visual":"Image GV-L10-U1-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"In formal English, when a negative or restrictive adverbial comes at the start of a sentence for emphasis, the word order changes to question order: adverbial + auxiliary + subject + main verb. Normal: Schools had never faced such a challenge. Inverted: Never before had schools faced such a challenge. Common adverbials: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Little, Nowhere, At no time, Under no circumstances, On no account. Two-part patterns: Not only + aux + subject…, but (subject) also…; Hardly / Scarcely + had + subject + past participle + when…; No sooner + had + subject + past participle + than….","on_screen":"Negative adverbial + auxiliary + subject + verb • no auxiliary → do / does / did + subject + base verb • Hardly / Scarcely… when • No sooner… than • Not only…, but also","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Never have I met such a patient teacher. Rarely do students enjoy exams. Not only did she pass the course, but she also won a scholarship.","on_screen":"Never have I met such a patient teacher. / Rarely do students enjoy exams. / Not only did she pass the course, but she also won a scholarship.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Never I have seen such a beautiful school.” That’s not right. We say: “Never have I seen such a beautiful school.” Inversion: auxiliary before the subject.","on_screen":"✗ Never I have seen such a beautiful school.   ✓ Never have I seen such a beautiful school.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: \"Never before had schools faced such a challenge.\" Is this a question? … Think! … No – it's an emphatic statement. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"Never before had schools faced such a challenge.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"Never before had schools faced such a challenge.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: inversion (auxiliary + subject + verb) after negative and restrictive adverbials at the start of a sentence: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Not only… but also, Hardly / Scarcely… when, No sooner… than, Under no circumstances / On no account / At no time, Little, Nowhere; adding do/does/did when there is no auxiliary.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","عندما يأتي ظرف منفي أو مقيِّد في أول الجملة للتوكيد، يتغيّر ترتيب الكلمات إلى ترتيب السؤال: الظرف + الفعل المساعد + الفاعل + الفعل الرئيس: Never before had schools faced such a challenge.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Never I have seen such a beautiful school. — الصحيح: Never have I seen such a beautiful school.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب Never before had schools faced such a challenge."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Learning Without Walls","body":"Never before had Saudi schools faced a challenge like the one in March 2020. Hardly had students settled into the new term when classrooms across the Kingdom closed because of the pandemic. Within weeks, millions of students were learning online through a national platform called Madrasati.\nNot only did teachers have to learn new technology, but they also had to rethink the way they taught. Seldom had so many people changed their habits so quickly. Some students thrived; others struggled without the structure of a normal school day.\nLittle did anyone know at the time that this crisis would change education permanently. When students returned to their classrooms, many teachers continued to use the digital tools they had discovered. Nowhere is this clearer than in the way homework is now set and submitted online.\nYet experts warn that technology alone cannot guarantee learning. Under no circumstances should screens replace the relationship between a teacher and a student. Only when students are curious, motivated and supported do they truly learn.\nWhat, then, will the classroom of tomorrow look like? Rarely do educators agree on everything, but most believe that future learners will need more than knowledge. They will need to think critically, work in teams and keep learning throughout their lives. No sooner do we master one skill than the world asks for another. Lifelong learning, therefore, is no longer a choice; it is a necessity.","word_count":235,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Never before ___ such a challenge.","options":["had faced Saudi schools","did Saudi schools faced","had Saudi schools faced","Saudi schools had faced"],"answer":"had Saudi schools faced","explanation":"Never / Rarely / Seldom + auxiliary + subject.","explanation_ar":"Never have I."},{"q":"Hardly had students settled into the term ___ classrooms closed.","options":["then","than","when","that"],"answer":"when","explanation":"Hardly… when / No sooner… than.","explanation_ar":"Hardly… when."},{"q":"Not only ___ new technology, but they also changed how they taught.","options":["teachers learned","teachers did learn","learned teachers","did teachers learn"],"answer":"did teachers learn","explanation":"Not only + auxiliary + subject…, but also…","explanation_ar":"Not only… but also."},{"q":"Little ___ that the crisis would change education forever.","options":["did anyone know","anyone knew","anyone did know","knew anyone"],"answer":"did anyone know","explanation":"Little + did + subject + know / realize.","explanation_ar":"Little did he know."},{"q":"Under no circumstances ___ replace the relationship between a teacher and a student.","options":["screens should","screens should not","should screens to","should screens"],"answer":"should screens","explanation":"Under no circumstances / At no time / Nowhere + auxiliary + subject.","explanation_ar":"Under no circumstances."},{"q":"Seldom ______ a single invention transform education as quickly as the internet did in the early twenty-first century.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["it had","has","had it","it has"],"answer":"has","explanation":"Never / Rarely / Seldom + auxiliary + subject.","explanation_ar":"Never have I."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite with the adverbial at the start.","items":[{"q":"I have never met such a patient teacher. (Never)  (inversion)","options":[],"answer":"Never have I met such a patient teacher.","explanation":"Never / Rarely / Seldom + auxiliary + subject.","explanation_ar":"Never have I."},{"q":"Students rarely enjoy exams. (Rarely)  (inversion with do)","options":[],"answer":"Rarely do students enjoy exams.","explanation":"Add do / does / did when there is no auxiliary.","explanation_ar":"إضافة do / did."},{"q":"The bell rang, and immediately everyone left. (No sooner)  (No sooner… than)","options":[],"answer":"No sooner had the bell rung than everyone left.","explanation":"Hardly… when / No sooner… than.","explanation_ar":"Hardly… when."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"Never I have seen such a beautiful campus.","options":[],"answer":"Never have I seen such a beautiful campus.","explanation":"Never I have → Never have I. Never / Rarely / Seldom + auxiliary + subject.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Never I have → Never have I. Never have I."},{"q":"Rarely students fail this course.","options":[],"answer":"Rarely do students fail this course.","explanation":"Rarely students → Rarely do students. Add do / does / did when there is no auxiliary.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Rarely students → Rarely do students. إضافة do / did."},{"q":"No sooner had the exam started when the fire alarm rang.","options":[],"answer":"No sooner had the exam started than the fire alarm rang.","explanation":"when → than. Hardly… when / No sooner… than.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: when → than. Hardly… when."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Emphasize your experiences.","items":[{"q":"Begin with \"Never have I…\" about school.","options":[],"answer":"Never have I enjoyed a subject as much as chemistry.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion (auxiliary + subject + verb) after negative and restrictive adverbials at the start of a sentence: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Not only… but also, Hardly / Scarcely… when, No sooner… than, Under no circumstances / On no account / At no time, Little, Nowhere; adding do/does/did when there is no auxiliary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Begin with \"Not only… but also…\" about a teacher.","options":[],"answer":"Not only does my math teacher explain clearly, but she also makes us laugh.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion (auxiliary + subject + verb) after negative and restrictive adverbials at the start of a sentence: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Not only… but also, Hardly / Scarcely… when, No sooner… than, Under no circumstances / On no account / At no time, Little, Nowhere; adding do/does/did when there is no auxiliary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Begin with \"Little did I know…\".","options":[],"answer":"Little did I know that my first coding class would change my career plans.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion (auxiliary + subject + verb) after negative and restrictive adverbials at the start of a sentence: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Not only… but also, Hardly / Scarcely… when, No sooner… than, Under no circumstances / On no account / At no time, Little, Nowhere; adding do/does/did when there is no auxiliary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Begin with \"Under no circumstances should…\" for a school rule.","options":[],"answer":"Under no circumstances should students use phones during exams.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion (auxiliary + subject + verb) after negative and restrictive adverbials at the start of a sentence: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Not only… but also, Hardly / Scarcely… when, No sooner… than, Under no circumstances / On no account / At no time, Little, Nowhere; adding do/does/did when there is no auxiliary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Begin with \"Hardly had… when…\".","options":[],"answer":"Hardly had I opened my book when my little brother started crying.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion (auxiliary + subject + verb) after negative and restrictive adverbials at the start of a sentence: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Not only… but also, Hardly / Scarcely… when, No sooner… than, Under no circumstances / On no account / At no time, Little, Nowhere; adding do/does/did when there is no auxiliary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: A speech to new students.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 emphatic sentences with inversion welcoming new students.","options":[],"answer":"Never has our school welcomed such a talented group. Not only will you learn here, but you will also make friends for life.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion (auxiliary + subject + verb) after negative and restrictive adverbials at the start of a sentence: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Not only… but also, Hardly / Scarcely… when, No sooner… than, Under no circumstances / On no account / At no time, Little, Nowhere; adding do/does/did when there is no auxiliary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 school rules with inversion.","options":[],"answer":"Under no circumstances should you copy someone else's work. At no time should phones be used in the laboratory.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion (auxiliary + subject + verb) after negative and restrictive adverbials at the start of a sentence: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Not only… but also, Hardly / Scarcely… when, No sooner… than, Under no circumstances / On no account / At no time, Little, Nowhere; adding do/does/did when there is no auxiliary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with \"Rarely…\" about learning.","options":[],"answer":"Rarely does real learning happen without mistakes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion (auxiliary + subject + verb) after negative and restrictive adverbials at the start of a sentence: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Not only… but also, Hardly / Scarcely… when, No sooner… than, Under no circumstances / On no account / At no time, Little, Nowhere; adding do/does/did when there is no auxiliary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Four Corners Grammar","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a sentence frame with a cue word and four possible answers (A–D).","Students walk to the corner with the correct answer.","One student in each corner explains the choice in one sentence.","Correct corner scores a point; continue with the next cue."],"data":[{"label":"Never have I…"},{"label":"Rarely do…"},{"label":"Not only did…, but… also"},{"label":"Hardly had… when…"},{"label":"No sooner had… than…"},{"label":"Under no circumstances should…"},{"label":"Only when… do…"},{"label":"So… was… that…"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Rarely ___ a student finish this exam in less than an hour.","options":["do","has it","is","does"],"answer":"does","explanation":"Add do / does / did when there is no auxiliary.","explanation_ar":"إضافة do / did."},{"q":"Seldom ___ such a well-organized conference.","options":["have attended I","I have attended","have I attended","I attended"],"answer":"have I attended","explanation":"Never / Rarely / Seldom + auxiliary + subject.","explanation_ar":"Never have I."},{"q":"Not only ___ the exam, but she also got the highest mark.","options":["did she pass","she passed","passed she","she did pass"],"answer":"did she pass","explanation":"Not only + auxiliary + subject…, but also…","explanation_ar":"Not only… but also."},{"q":"No sooner ___ the results than he called his parents.","options":["had he received","he received","he had received","did he received"],"answer":"had he received","explanation":"Hardly… when / No sooner… than.","explanation_ar":"Hardly… when."},{"q":"","options":["At no time the teacher lost her patience.","At no time did the teacher lose her patience.","At no time did the teacher lost her patience.","At no time the teacher did lose her patience."],"answer":"At no time did the teacher lose her patience.","explanation":"Under no circumstances / At no time / Nowhere + auxiliary + subject.","explanation_ar":"Under no circumstances."},{"q":"","options":["Little did we realized how difficult the course would be.","Little we realized how difficult the course would be.","Little did we realize how difficult the course would be.","Little realized we how difficult the course would be."],"answer":"Little did we realize how difficult the course would be.","explanation":"Little + did + subject + know / realize.","explanation_ar":"Little did he know."},{"q":"Hardly ___ when the professor's microphone stopped working.","options":["did the lecture begun","the lecture had begun","had the lecture begun","had begun the lecture"],"answer":"had the lecture begun","explanation":"Hardly… when / No sooner… than.","explanation_ar":"Hardly… when."},{"q":"Nowhere ______ the benefits of reading more visible than in students' writing, which becomes richer and more precise.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["it is","they are","is","are"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Under no circumstances / At no time / Nowhere + auxiliary + subject.","explanation_ar":"Under no circumstances."},{"q":"Not only ______ millions of students during the pandemic, but it also became a permanent part of the school system.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["did the national platform serve","the national platform did serve","the national platform served","served the national platform"],"answer":"did the national platform serve","explanation":"Not only + auxiliary + subject…, but also…","explanation_ar":"Not only… but also."},{"q":"\"Never have I seen such dedication.\" What effect does the inversion create?","options":["a negative command","strong, formal emphasis","a question","a future plan"],"answer":"strong, formal emphasis","explanation":"Never / Rarely / Seldom + auxiliary + subject.","explanation_ar":"Never have I."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"A Saudi student studying at home in 2020 on a laptop showing an online class platform, and a split image of the same student back in a modern classroom in 2024 using a tablet in a group project, with a teacher guiding the discussion. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A Saudi student studying at home in 2020 on a laptop showing an online class platform, and a split image of the same student back in a modern classroom in 2024 using a tablet in a group project, with a teacher guiding the discussion"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about inversion (auxiliary + subject + verb) after negative and restrictive adverbials at the start of a sentence: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Not only… but also, Hardly / Scarcely… when, No sooner… than, Under no circumstances / On no account / At no time, Little, Nowhere; adding do/does/did when there is no auxiliary, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about inversion (auxiliary + subject + verb) after negative and restrictive adverbials at the start of a sentence: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Not only… but also, Hardly / Scarcely… when, No sooner… than, Under no circumstances / On no account / At no time, Little, Nowhere"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows curriculum (all the subjects and content taught in a school or course); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing curriculum: all the subjects and content taught in a school or course"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows platform (a digital system or website used for a particular purpose); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing platform: a digital system or website used for a particular purpose"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows thrive (to grow, develop or be successful); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing thrive: to grow, develop or be successful"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows lifelong learning (continuing to learn throughout your life); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing lifelong learning: continuing to learn throughout your life"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Four Corners Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Four Corners Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS1-W01","script":"curriculum. curriculum. The new curriculum includes coding from Grade 4.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS1-W02","script":"platform. platform. Students submit their homework on an online platform.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS1-W03","script":"thrive. thrive. Some students thrive in online classes.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS1-W04","script":"lifelong learning. lifelong learning. Lifelong learning helps people adapt to new jobs.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS1-T1","script":"Never before had Saudi schools faced a challenge like the one in March 2020. Hardly had students settled into the new term when classrooms across the Kingdom closed because of the pandemic. Within weeks, millions of students were learning online through a national platform called Madrasati. Not only did teachers have to learn new technology, but they also had to rethink the way they taught. Seldom had so many people changed their habits so quickly. Some students thrived; others struggled without the structure of a normal school day. Little did anyone know at the time that this crisis would change education permanently. When students returned to their classrooms, many teachers continued to use the digital tools they had discovered. Nowhere is this clearer than in the way homework is now set and submitted online. Yet experts warn that technology alone cannot guarantee learning. Under no circumstances should screens replace the relationship between a teacher and a student. Only when students are curious, motivated and supported do they truly learn. What, then, will the classroom of tomorrow look like? Rarely do educators agree on everything, but most believe that future learners will need more than knowledge. They will need to think critically, work in teams and keep learning throughout their lives. No sooner do we master one skill than the world asks for another. Lifelong learning, therefore, is no longer a choice; it is a necessity.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Never Before Had Schools Faced Such a Challenge: Inversion After Negative Adverbials”. Let’s learn inversion (auxiliary + subject + verb) after negative and restrictive adverbials at the start of a sentence: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Not only… but also, Hardly / Scarcely… when, No sooner… than, Under no circumstances / On no account / At no time, Little, Nowhere; adding do/does/did when there is no auxiliary together. Listen to the start of “Learning Without Walls”: Never before had Saudi schools faced a challenge like the one in March 2020. Hardly had students settled into the new term when classrooms across the Kingdom closed because of the pandemic. Within weeks, millions of students were learning online through a national platform called Madrasati. Not only did teachers have to learn new technology, but they also had to rethink the way they taught. Seldom had so many people changed their habits so quickly. Look at the green words. In formal English, when a negative or restrictive adverbial comes at the start of a sentence for emphasis, the word order changes to question order: adverbial + auxiliary + subject + main verb. Normal: Schools had never faced such a challenge. Inverted: Never before had schools faced such a challenge. Common adverbials: Never (before), Rarely, Seldom, Little, Nowhere, At no time, Under no circumstances, On no account. Two-part patterns: Not only + aux + subject…, but (subject) also…; Hardly / Scarcely + had + subject + past participle + when…; No sooner + had + subject + past participle + than…. Here are some examples. Never have I met such a patient teacher. Rarely do students enjoy exams. Not only did she pass the course, but she also won a scholarship. Be careful! Some learners say: “Never I have seen such a beautiful school.” That’s not right. We say: “Never have I seen such a beautiful school.” Inversion: auxiliary before the subject. Quick check: \"Never before had schools faced such a challenge.\" Is this a question? … Think! … No – it's an emphatic statement. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"Never before had schools faced such a challenge.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.05"}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2","title":"Only When Students Are Curious Do They Learn: Inversion with only, so and such","objectives":["Students will be able to use inversion after only and not until, inverting the main clause.","Students will be able to use so… that and such… that inversion for dramatic emphasis.","I can write \"Only when we ask questions do we truly learn.\"","I can write \"So difficult was the exam that few students passed.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام التقديم والتأخير بعد only وnot until مع قلب الجملة الرئيسة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام so… that وsuch… that مع التقديم للتوكيد البلاغي.","أستطيع أن أكتب Only when we ask questions do we truly learn.","أستطيع أن أكتب So difficult was the exam that few students passed."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"assessment","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈsɛsmənt/","definition":"the process of testing and judging students' learning","arabic":"تقييم","example":"The course has three assessments and a final exam.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS2-W01"},{"word":"literacy","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlɪtɚəsi/","definition":"the ability to read and write; knowledge of a particular area","arabic":"محو الأمية / المعرفة بمجال","example":"Digital literacy is essential today.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS2-W02"},{"word":"vocational","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/voʊˈkeɪʃənəl/","definition":"teaching the skills needed for a particular job","arabic":"مهني","example":"He chose a vocational course in electrical engineering.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS2-W03"},{"word":"enroll","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɛnˈroʊl/","definition":"to officially join a school, course or program","arabic":"يلتحق / يسجّل","example":"She enrolled in an online programming course.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"After Only + time / condition expression at the start, invert the main clause (not the only-clause): Only when students are curious do they learn. Only after the results were published did we celebrate. Only by practicing every day can you improve. Only then did I understand. Only if you study will you pass.\nNot until works the same way: Not until the final week did he start revising. The clause after Not until / Only when keeps normal word order; the main clause is inverted.\nFor dramatic emphasis, put so + adjective/adverb at the start and invert: So difficult was the exam that few students passed. So quickly did she finish that the teacher was surprised. Such + be + noun + that: Such was the demand for places that the university opened a new campus.\nOnly when / after / by / if / then… + auxiliary + subject (main clause)\nNot until… + auxiliary + subject (main clause)\nSo + adjective + be + subject + that… • So + adverb + auxiliary + subject + verb + that…\nSuch + be + noun phrase + that…","examples":["Only when we make mistakes do we learn to think critically.","Only after she had finished her degree did she start her company.","Only by working together can we solve this problem.","Not until the results came out did he believe he had passed.","So rigorous was the course that only half the students completed it.","So fast did he type that he finished the essay in an hour.","Such was the success of the program that it was expanded nationwide.","Only then did I understand the value of lifelong learning."],"common_errors":["✗ Only when students are curious they learn. → ✓ Only when students are curious do they learn. (Invert the main clause.)","✗ Only when are students curious do they learn. → ✓ Only when students are curious do they learn. (Normal order in the only-clause.)","✗ So difficult the exam was that few passed. → ✓ So difficult was the exam that few passed. (Invert after so + adjective.)","✗ Not until the end he realized his mistake. → ✓ Not until the end did he realize his mistake. (Inversion with did.)"],"arabic":"بعد Only + تعبير زمن أو شرط في أول الجملة نقلب الجملة الرئيسة لا جملة only: Only when students are curious do they learn.\nNot until تعمل بالطريقة نفسها: Not until the final week did he start revising.\nللتوكيد البلاغي: So + صفة + be + الفاعل + that: So difficult was the exam that few students passed.\nوSuch + be + اسم + that: Such was the demand that the university opened a new campus."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Only When Students Are Curious Do They Learn: Inversion with only, so and such”. Let’s learn inversion after only + time/condition expressions (Only when…, Only after…, Only by…, Only then…, Only if…) and Not until…; inversion in the main clause; so + adjective/adverb + auxiliary + subject + that…; Such + be + noun + that… together.","on_screen":"GV-L10-U1-LS2 | Only When Students Are Curious Do They Learn: Inversion with only, so and such","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: Only by reading widely can you develop a rich vocabulary. Not until he failed did he realize the course was rigorous. (These are emphatic statements, not questions.)","on_screen":"Only by reading widely can you develop a rich vocabulary. | Not until he failed did he realize the course was rigorous. | (These are emphatic statements, not questions.)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"After Only + time / condition expression at the start, invert the main clause (not the only-clause): Only when students are curious do they learn. Only after the results were published did we celebrate. Only by practicing every day can you improve. Only then did I understand. Only if you study will you pass. Not until works the same way: Not until the final week did he start revising. The clause after Not until / Only when keeps normal word order; the main clause is inverted.","on_screen":"Only when / after / by / if / then… + auxiliary + subject (main clause) • Not until… + auxiliary + subject (main clause) • So + adjective + be + subject + that… • So + adverb + auxiliary + subject + verb + that…","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Only when we make mistakes do we learn to think critically. Only after she had finished her degree did she start her company. Only by working together can we solve this problem.","on_screen":"Only when we make mistakes do we learn to think critically. / Only after she had finished her degree did she start her company. / Only by working together can we solve this problem.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Only when students are curious they learn.” That’s not right. We say: “Only when students are curious do they learn.” Invert the main clause.","on_screen":"✗ Only when students are curious they learn.   ✓ Only when students are curious do they learn.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: \"Only when students are curious do they learn.\" Which clause is inverted? … Think! … The main clause: *do they learn*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"Only when we ask questions do we truly learn.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"Only when we ask questions do we truly learn.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: inversion after only + time/condition expressions (Only when…, Only after…, Only by…, Only then…, Only if…) and Not until…; inversion in the main clause; so + adjective/adverb + auxiliary + subject + that…; Such + be + noun + that….","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","بعد Only + تعبير زمن أو شرط في أول الجملة نقلب الجملة الرئيسة لا جملة only: Only when students are curious do they learn.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Only when students are curious they learn. — الصحيح: Only when students are curious do they learn.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب Only when we ask questions do we truly learn."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Only when students are curious ___ truly learn.","options":["do they","are they","they","they do"],"answer":"do they","explanation":"Only when / after / if + main-clause inversion.","explanation_ar":"Only when."},{"q":"Only by practicing every day ___ your English.","options":["you can improve","you improve can","can you improve","improve you can"],"answer":"can you improve","explanation":"Only by / Only then + inversion.","explanation_ar":"Only by."},{"q":"Not until the final week ___ revising for the exam.","options":["he did start","started he","he started","did he start"],"answer":"did he start","explanation":"Not until + main-clause inversion.","explanation_ar":"Not until."},{"q":"So difficult ___ that only a few students passed.","options":["was the exam","the exam did","the exam was","did the exam"],"answer":"was the exam","explanation":"So + adjective/adverb + inversion + that.","explanation_ar":"So… that."},{"q":"___ was the demand for places that the university opened a new campus.","options":["So","Such","So much","Such a"],"answer":"Such","explanation":"Such + be + noun + that.","explanation_ar":"Such… that."},{"q":"Only after the scientists had repeated the experiment several times ______ their results to the journal.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["submitted they","did they submit","they submitted","they did submit"],"answer":"did they submit","explanation":"Only when / after / if + main-clause inversion.","explanation_ar":"Only when."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite with the words in brackets at the start.","items":[{"q":"You can succeed only if you work hard. (Only if)  (inversion)","options":[],"answer":"Only if you work hard can you succeed.","explanation":"Only when / after / if + main-clause inversion.","explanation_ar":"Only when."},{"q":"He realized his mistake only after the exam. (Only after)  (inversion)","options":[],"answer":"Only after the exam did he realize his mistake.","explanation":"Only when / after / if + main-clause inversion.","explanation_ar":"Only when."},{"q":"The course was so popular that it was repeated. (So popular)  (so… that)","options":[],"answer":"So popular was the course that it was repeated.","explanation":"So + adjective/adverb + inversion + that.","explanation_ar":"So… that."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"Only when the bell rang the students left.","options":[],"answer":"Only when the bell rang did the students leave.","explanation":"the students left → did the students leave. Normal order in the only/until clause; invert the main clause.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: the students left → did the students leave. قلب الجملة الرئيسة فقط."},{"q":"So quickly she finished that the teacher was surprised.","options":[],"answer":"So quickly did she finish that the teacher was surprised.","explanation":"So quickly she finished → So quickly did she finish. So + adjective/adverb + inversion + that.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: So quickly she finished → So quickly did she finish. So… that."},{"q":"Not until the results came out he believed he had passed.","options":[],"answer":"Not until the results came out did he believe he had passed.","explanation":"he believed → did he believe. Not until + main-clause inversion.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: he believed → did he believe. Not until."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Express conditions and emphasis.","items":[{"q":"Begin with \"Only by…\" to give study advice.","options":[],"answer":"Only by reading every day can you build a strong vocabulary.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after only + time/condition expressions (Only when…, Only after…, Only by…, Only then…, Only if…) and Not until…; inversion in the main clause; so + adjective/adverb + auxiliary + subject + that…; Such + be + noun + that… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Begin with \"Only when…\" about understanding.","options":[],"answer":"Only when I teach a topic to someone else do I really understand it.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after only + time/condition expressions (Only when…, Only after…, Only by…, Only then…, Only if…) and Not until…; inversion in the main clause; so + adjective/adverb + auxiliary + subject + that…; Such + be + noun + that… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Begin with \"Not until…\" about a realization.","options":[],"answer":"Not until I failed my first quiz did I start taking notes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after only + time/condition expressions (Only when…, Only after…, Only by…, Only then…, Only if…) and Not until…; inversion in the main clause; so + adjective/adverb + auxiliary + subject + that…; Such + be + noun + that… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Begin with \"So + adjective…\" about a memorable day.","options":[],"answer":"So exciting was the science fair that nobody wanted to go home.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after only + time/condition expressions (Only when…, Only after…, Only by…, Only then…, Only if…) and Not until…; inversion in the main clause; so + adjective/adverb + auxiliary + subject + that…; Such + be + noun + that… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Begin with \"Such was…\".","options":[],"answer":"Such was my excitement that I couldn't sleep the night before the trip.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after only + time/condition expressions (Only when…, Only after…, Only by…, Only then…, Only if…) and Not until…; inversion in the main clause; so + adjective/adverb + auxiliary + subject + that…; Such + be + noun + that… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Graduation speech.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 sentences with \"Only…\" inversion about what students have learned.","options":[],"answer":"Only by facing challenges did we discover our strengths. Only now do we understand how much our teachers gave us.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after only + time/condition expressions (Only when…, Only after…, Only by…, Only then…, Only if…) and Not until…; inversion in the main clause; so + adjective/adverb + auxiliary + subject + that…; Such + be + noun + that… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one \"So… that\" and one \"Such… that\" sentence about the school year.","options":[],"answer":"So quickly did the year pass that it feels like a week. Such was our team spirit that we won every competition.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after only + time/condition expressions (Only when…, Only after…, Only by…, Only then…, Only if…) and Not until…; inversion in the main clause; so + adjective/adverb + auxiliary + subject + that…; Such + be + noun + that… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with \"Not until…\".","options":[],"answer":"Not until today did I realize how much I will miss this school.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after only + time/condition expressions (Only when…, Only after…, Only by…, Only then…, Only if…) and Not until…; inversion in the main clause; so + adjective/adverb + auxiliary + subject + that…; Such + be + noun + that… correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Snakes & Ladders","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Roll and move. If you land on a cue square, make a sentence with the cue and inversion after only + time/condition expressions (Only when…, Only after…, Only by…, Only then…, Only if…) and Not until…; inversion in the main clause; so + adjective/adverb + auxiliary + subject + that…; Such + be + noun + that….","Correct at the bottom of a ladder: climb. Incorrect at the head of a snake: slide down.","Teammates are the judges and must explain any correction.","First player to reach square 30 wins."],"data":[{"cue":"I / never / see / such a patient teacher (Never have I)"},{"cue":"students / rarely / enjoy / exams (Rarely do)"},{"cue":"she / pass / and / win a prize (Not only did)"},{"cue":"we / hardly / start / the test / when / the alarm / ring"},{"cue":"the bell / no sooner / ring / than / everyone / leave"},{"cue":"you / under no circumstances / copy / answers"},{"cue":"only when / we / ask questions / we / learn"},{"cue":"so / difficult / be / the exam / that / few passed"},{"cue":"little / he / know / that / he / would become a professor"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Only after he had graduated ___ the value of his teachers' advice.","options":["did he appreciate","appreciated he","he did appreciate","he appreciated"],"answer":"did he appreciate","explanation":"Only when / after / if + main-clause inversion.","explanation_ar":"Only when."},{"q":"Only then ___ how much she had learned.","options":["did she realize","she realized","realized she","she did realize"],"answer":"did she realize","explanation":"Only by / Only then + inversion.","explanation_ar":"Only by."},{"q":"Not until I moved abroad ___ to cook for myself.","options":["I learned","I did learn","learned I","did I learn"],"answer":"did I learn","explanation":"Not until + main-clause inversion.","explanation_ar":"Not until."},{"q":"So quickly ___ that the teacher thought she had cheated.","options":["she did finish","did she finish","she finished","finished she"],"answer":"did she finish","explanation":"So + adjective/adverb + inversion + that.","explanation_ar":"So… that."},{"q":"Such ___ the success of the program that it was introduced in every school.","options":["did","had","was","were"],"answer":"was","explanation":"Such + be + noun + that.","explanation_ar":"Such… that."},{"q":"","options":["Only when students feel safe they do ask questions.","Only when do students feel safe they ask questions.","Only when students feel safe do they ask questions.","Only when students feel safe they ask questions."],"answer":"Only when students feel safe do they ask questions.","explanation":"Normal order in the only/until clause; invert the main clause.","explanation_ar":"قلب الجملة الرئيسة فقط."},{"q":"","options":["So rigorous was the program that only ten students completed it.","So rigorous did the program that only ten students completed it.","So rigorous the program was that only ten students completed it.","Such rigorous was the program that only ten students completed it."],"answer":"So rigorous was the program that only ten students completed it.","explanation":"So + adjective/adverb + inversion + that.","explanation_ar":"So… that."},{"q":"Only if a student meets all the requirements ______ for the scholarship, which covers tuition for four years.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["he or she apply can","can he or she apply","he or she can apply","applies he or she"],"answer":"can he or she apply","explanation":"Only when / after / if + main-clause inversion.","explanation_ar":"Only when."},{"q":"So successful ______ that the ministry decided to expand it to every region of the country.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["the reading program was","did the reading program","the reading program did","was the reading program"],"answer":"was the reading program","explanation":"So + adjective/adverb + inversion + that.","explanation_ar":"So… that."},{"q":"In \"Only by working together can we solve this problem,\" which part keeps normal word order?","options":["this problem can","we solve this","by working together","can we solve"],"answer":"by working together","explanation":"Normal order in the only/until clause; invert the main clause.","explanation_ar":"قلب الجملة الرئيسة فقط."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A university lecture hall during a challenging final exam: students concentrating; on the board \"Only by practicing do you improve\" and \"So rigorous was the course that…\"; a professor walking between the rows. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A university lecture hall during a challenging final exam: students concentrating; on the board \"Only by practicing do you improve\" and \"So rigorous was the course that…\"; a professor walking between the rows"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of inversion after only + time/condition expressions (Only when…, Only after…, Only by…, Only then…, Only if…) and Not until…; inversion in the main clause; so + adjective/adverb + auxiliary + subject + that…; Such + be + noun + that…: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Learning for Tomorrow”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of inversion after only + time/condition expressions (Only when…, Only after…, Only by…, Only then…, Only if…) and Not until…"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows assessment (the process of testing and judging students' learning); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing assessment: the process of testing and judging students' learning"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows literacy (the ability to read and write; knowledge of a particular area); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing literacy: the ability to read and write; knowledge of a particular area"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows vocational (teaching the skills needed for a particular job); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing vocational: teaching the skills needed for a particular job"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows enroll (to officially join a school, course or program); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing enroll: to officially join a school, course or program"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Snakes & Ladders”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Snakes & Ladders"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS2-W01","script":"assessment. assessment. The course has three assessments and a final exam.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS2-W02","script":"literacy. literacy. Digital literacy is essential today.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS2-W03","script":"vocational. vocational. He chose a vocational course in electrical engineering.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS2-W04","script":"enroll. enroll. She enrolled in an online programming course.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Only When Students Are Curious Do They Learn: Inversion with only, so and such”. Let’s learn inversion after only + time/condition expressions (Only when…, Only after…, Only by…, Only then…, Only if…) and Not until…; inversion in the main clause; so + adjective/adverb + auxiliary + subject + that…; Such + be + noun + that… together. Remember these patterns: Only by reading widely can you develop a rich vocabulary. Not until he failed did he realize the course was rigorous. (These are emphatic statements, not questions.) After Only + time / condition expression at the start, invert the main clause (not the only-clause): Only when students are curious do they learn. Only after the results were published did we celebrate. Only by practicing every day can you improve. Only then did I understand. Only if you study will you pass. Not until works the same way: Not until the final week did he start revising. The clause after Not until / Only when keeps normal word order; the main clause is inverted. Here are some examples. Only when we make mistakes do we learn to think critically. Only after she had finished her degree did she start her company. Only by working together can we solve this problem. Be careful! Some learners say: “Only when students are curious they learn.” That’s not right. We say: “Only when students are curious do they learn.” Invert the main clause. Quick check: \"Only when students are curious do they learn.\" Which clause is inverted? … Think! … The main clause: *do they learn*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"Only when we ask questions do we truly learn.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.05"}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3","title":"Acquire Knowledge, Think Critically: Education Vocabulary and Academic Collocations","objectives":["Students will be able to use education vocabulary and academic collocations accurately.","Students will be able to choose formal academic words instead of informal ones in writing.","I can say \"enroll in a program\", \"submit an assignment\" and \"conduct research\".","I can explain what plagiarism is and why it matters."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام مفردات التعليم والمتلازمات الأكاديمية بدقة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من اختيار الكلمات الأكاديمية الرسمية بدلًا من غير الرسمية في الكتابة.","أستطيع أن أقول enroll in a program وsubmit an assignment وconduct research.","أستطيع أن أشرح ما هي السرقة الأدبية ولماذا هي مهمة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"tuition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tjuˈɪʃən/","definition":"the money you pay to study, or teaching itself","arabic":"الرسوم الدراسية","example":"Many universities offer free tuition to top students.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-W01"},{"word":"dropout","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdrɑˌpaʊt/","definition":"a student who leaves school before finishing","arabic":"منقطع عن الدراسة","example":"The program helps dropouts return to education.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-W02"},{"word":"critical thinking","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˈkrɪtɪkəl ˈθɪŋkɪŋ/","definition":"the ability to analyze information carefully before you decide","arabic":"التفكير الناقد","example":"Critical thinking helps us recognize misinformation.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-W03"},{"word":"plagiarism","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpleɪdʒɚˌɪzəm/","definition":"copying someone else's work and presenting it as your own","arabic":"السرقة الأدبية / الانتحال","example":"Plagiarism is a serious offense at university.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-W04"},{"word":"rigorous","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈrɪɡɚəs/","definition":"very careful, thorough and demanding","arabic":"صارم / دقيق","example":"Medical schools have rigorous admission tests.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-W05"},{"word":"discipline","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdɪsəplən/","definition":"a subject or field of study","arabic":"تخصص / مجال معرفي","example":"Engineering is a demanding discipline.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-W06"},{"word":"competence","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɑmpətɪns/","definition":"the ability to do something well","arabic":"كفاءة","example":"Employers look for competence in communication.","image_id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-W07","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-W07"}],"explanation":{"text":"Academic collocations: acquire / gain knowledge; develop critical thinking / skills; enroll in a course / a program; pursue a degree; major in a subject; attend lectures; submit an assignment; meet a deadline / the requirements; conduct / carry out research; take / sit an exam; improve academic performance; award a scholarship; avoid plagiarism; rigorous standards.\nEducation words: curriculum (all subjects taught), assessment (testing), literacy (reading and writing; or knowledge of a field: digital literacy), vocational (job-skills) education, tuition (fees), dropout (someone who leaves school early), discipline (a field of study), competence (ability), plagiarism (copying others' work).\nIn academic writing, choose formal words: obtain (not get), investigate (not look into), demonstrate (not show), require (not need), significant (not big), numerous (not lots of). Word families: assess → assessment; compete → competence → competent; educate → education → educational → educator.\nCollocations/phrases: acquire knowledge • develop critical thinking • pursue a degree • major in a subject | enroll in a program • attend lectures • submit an assignment • meet the requirements | conduct research • sit an exam • improve academic performance • avoid plagiarism | award a scholarship • rigorous standards • lifelong learning • digital literacy","examples":["She enrolled in a vocational program in renewable energy.","He is pursuing a degree in computer science.","All assignments must be submitted before midnight.","The students conducted research on water use in their school.","Digital literacy is now part of the national curriculum.","Copying from a website without citing it is plagiarism.","Medical schools have rigorous admission standards.","Critical thinking is a key competence for the future."],"common_errors":["✗ I want to make a degree in engineering. → ✓ I want to pursue / earn a degree in engineering. (pursue / earn a degree.)","✗ She enrolled to the course last year. → ✓ She enrolled in the course last year. (enroll in.)","✗ We did a research about pollution. → ✓ We conducted research on pollution. (research is uncountable; conduct research.)","✗ The results show a big improvement. (academic) → ✓ The results demonstrate a significant improvement. (Formal vocabulary.)"],"arabic":"متلازمات أكاديمية: acquire knowledge (يكتسب المعرفة) وpursue a degree (يسعى لنيل درجة) وenroll in (يلتحق بـ) وsubmit an assignment (يسلّم واجبًا) وconduct research (يجري بحثًا).\nresearch اسم غير معدود فلا نقول a research، وenroll تأتي مع in.\nكلمات التعليم: curriculum (المنهج) وassessment (التقييم) وliteracy (القراءة والكتابة أو المعرفة بمجال) وvocational (مهني) وplagiarism (السرقة الأدبية).\nفي الكتابة الأكاديمية نختار الكلمات الرسمية: obtain بدل get، وdemonstrate بدل show، وsignificant بدل big."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Acquire Knowledge, Think Critically: Education Vocabulary and Academic Collocations”. Let’s learn education vocabulary and academic collocations (acquire knowledge, develop critical thinking, enroll in a program, pursue a degree, submit an assignment, conduct research, meet the requirements, academic performance, rigorous standards, avoid plagiarism); academic word families together.","on_screen":"GV-L10-U1-LS3 | Acquire Knowledge, Think Critically: Education Vocabulary and Academic Collocations","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. tuition: the money you pay to study, or teaching itself. dropout: a student who leaves school before finishing. critical thinking: the ability to analyze information carefully before you decide.","on_screen":"tuition | dropout | critical thinking","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Academic collocations: acquire / gain knowledge; develop critical thinking / skills; enroll in a course / a program; pursue a degree; major in a subject; attend lectures; submit an assignment; meet a deadline / the requirements; conduct / carry out research; take / sit an exam; improve academic performance; award a scholarship; avoid plagiarism; rigorous standards. Education words: curriculum (all subjects taught), assessment (testing), literacy (reading and writing; or knowledge of a field: digital literacy), vocational (job-skills) education, tuition (fees), dropout (someone who leaves school early), discipline (a field of study), competence (ability), plagiarism (copying others' work).","on_screen":"education vocabulary and academic collocations (acquire knowledge, develop critical thinking, enroll in a program, pursue a degree, submit an assignment, conduct research, meet the requirements, academic performance, rigorous standards, avoid plagiarism); academic word families","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. She enrolled in a vocational program in renewable energy. He is pursuing a degree in computer science. All assignments must be submitted before midnight.","on_screen":"She enrolled in a vocational program in renewable energy. / He is pursuing a degree in computer science. / All assignments must be submitted before midnight.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I want to make a degree in engineering.” That’s not right. We say: “I want to pursue / earn a degree in engineering.” pursue / earn a degree.","on_screen":"✗ I want to make a degree in engineering.   ✓ I want to pursue / earn a degree in engineering.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: Is \"research\" countable? … Think! … No – *conduct research*, not \"a research\". Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"enroll in a program\", \"submit an assignment\" and \"conduct research\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"enroll in a program\", \"submit an assignment\" and \"conduct research\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: education vocabulary and academic collocations (acquire knowledge, develop critical thinking, enroll in a program, pursue a degree, submit an assignment, conduct research, meet the requirements, academic performance, rigorous standards, avoid plagiarism); academic word families.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","متلازمات أكاديمية: acquire knowledge (يكتسب المعرفة) وpursue a degree (يسعى لنيل درجة) وenroll in (يلتحق بـ) وsubmit an assignment (يسلّم واجبًا) وconduct research (يجري بحثًا).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I want to make a degree in engineering. — الصحيح: I want to pursue / earn a degree in engineering.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول enroll in a program وsubmit an assignment وconduct research."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"She ___ in a vocational program in renewable energy.","options":["entered in","enrolled","joined to","registered at"],"answer":"enrolled","explanation":"Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."},{"q":"The students ___ research on water use in their school.","options":["made","took","conducted","did a"],"answer":"conducted","explanation":"Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."},{"q":"Copying from a website without citing the source is ___.","options":["plagiarism","competence","literacy","assessment"],"answer":"plagiarism","explanation":"Education word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"In an academic essay, which word is more formal than \"show\"?","options":["look","point","tell","demonstrate"],"answer":"demonstrate","explanation":"Formal academic word choice.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة الرسمية."},{"q":"Teachers need strong ___ in technology to use digital platforms effectively.","options":["competent","competence","competitive","compete"],"answer":"competence","explanation":"Word-family form.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"To prepare students for a world in which information is everywhere, the new curriculum focuses less on memorizing facts and more on ______, the ability to evaluate evidence and arguments carefully.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["critical thinking","tuition","plagiarism","vocational training"],"answer":"critical thinking","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the verb to its partner.","items":[{"q":"pursue","options":["a degree in medicine","a scholarship to the top students","lectures and seminars","an assignment before the deadline","the entry requirements","new knowledge and skills"],"answer":"a degree in medicine","explanation":"pursue → a degree in medicine. Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."},{"q":"submit","options":["a degree in medicine","a scholarship to the top students","lectures and seminars","an assignment before the deadline","the entry requirements","new knowledge and skills"],"answer":"an assignment before the deadline","explanation":"submit → an assignment before the deadline. Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."},{"q":"meet","options":["a degree in medicine","a scholarship to the top students","lectures and seminars","an assignment before the deadline","the entry requirements","new knowledge and skills"],"answer":"the entry requirements","explanation":"meet → the entry requirements. Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."},{"q":"acquire","options":["a degree in medicine","a scholarship to the top students","lectures and seminars","an assignment before the deadline","the entry requirements","new knowledge and skills"],"answer":"new knowledge and skills","explanation":"acquire → new knowledge and skills. Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."},{"q":"attend","options":["a degree in medicine","a scholarship to the top students","lectures and seminars","an assignment before the deadline","the entry requirements","new knowledge and skills"],"answer":"lectures and seminars","explanation":"attend → lectures and seminars. Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."},{"q":"award","options":["a degree in medicine","a scholarship to the top students","lectures and seminars","an assignment before the deadline","the entry requirements","new knowledge and skills"],"answer":"a scholarship to the top students","explanation":"award → a scholarship to the top students. Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Talk about education.","items":[{"q":"What would you like to major in, and why?","options":[],"answer":"I'd like to major in biology because I'm fascinated by genetics.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses education vocabulary and academic collocations (acquire knowledge, develop critical thinking, enroll in a program, pursue a degree, submit an assignment, conduct research, meet the requirements, academic performance, rigorous standards, avoid plagiarism); academic word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How can schools improve students' digital literacy?","options":[],"answer":"Schools can teach students how to evaluate online sources.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses education vocabulary and academic collocations (acquire knowledge, develop critical thinking, enroll in a program, pursue a degree, submit an assignment, conduct research, meet the requirements, academic performance, rigorous standards, avoid plagiarism); academic word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Why is plagiarism a serious problem?","options":[],"answer":"Plagiarism is dishonest, and it stops students from developing their own ideas.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses education vocabulary and academic collocations (acquire knowledge, develop critical thinking, enroll in a program, pursue a degree, submit an assignment, conduct research, meet the requirements, academic performance, rigorous standards, avoid plagiarism); academic word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Would you consider a vocational program? Why or why not?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, because vocational programs lead quickly to well-paid jobs.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses education vocabulary and academic collocations (acquire knowledge, develop critical thinking, enroll in a program, pursue a degree, submit an assignment, conduct research, meet the requirements, academic performance, rigorous standards, avoid plagiarism); academic word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"lifelong learning\".","options":[],"answer":"Lifelong learning helps people stay employable as technology changes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses education vocabulary and academic collocations (acquire knowledge, develop critical thinking, enroll in a program, pursue a degree, submit an assignment, conduct research, meet the requirements, academic performance, rigorous standards, avoid plagiarism); academic word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: An academic profile.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences about your educational goals using 3 academic collocations.","options":[],"answer":"I hope to pursue a degree in engineering. I want to conduct research on renewable energy. First, I need to meet the entry requirements.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses education vocabulary and academic collocations (acquire knowledge, develop critical thinking, enroll in a program, pursue a degree, submit an assignment, conduct research, meet the requirements, academic performance, rigorous standards, avoid plagiarism); academic word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Rewrite these informal sentences formally: \"We got lots of info. It shows a big change.\"","options":[],"answer":"We obtained a significant amount of information. It demonstrates a considerable change.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses education vocabulary and academic collocations (acquire knowledge, develop critical thinking, enroll in a program, pursue a degree, submit an assignment, conduct research, meet the requirements, academic performance, rigorous standards, avoid plagiarism); academic word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence about what makes a curriculum effective.","options":[],"answer":"An effective curriculum develops both knowledge and critical thinking.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses education vocabulary and academic collocations (acquire knowledge, develop critical thinking, enroll in a program, pursue a degree, submit an assignment, conduct research, meet the requirements, academic performance, rigorous standards, avoid plagiarism); academic word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Dominoes","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Deal the dominoes equally in teams of four.","Player 1 places a domino; the next player adds a domino whose word matches the open definition.","If you cannot play, pass.","The first player with no dominoes left wins."],"data":[{"word":"curriculum","match":"all the subjects and content taught in a school or course","arabic":"المنهج الدراسي"},{"word":"platform","match":"a digital system or website used for a particular purpose","arabic":"منصة"},{"word":"thrive","match":"to grow, develop or be successful","arabic":"يزدهر / ينجح"},{"word":"lifelong learning","match":"continuing to learn throughout your life","arabic":"التعلّم مدى الحياة"},{"word":"assessment","match":"the process of testing and judging students' learning","arabic":"تقييم"},{"word":"literacy","match":"the ability to read and write; knowledge of a particular area","arabic":"محو الأمية / المعرفة بمجال"},{"word":"vocational","match":"teaching the skills needed for a particular job","arabic":"مهني"},{"word":"enroll","match":"to officially join a school, course or program","arabic":"يلتحق / يسجّل"},{"word":"tuition","match":"the money you pay to study, or teaching itself","arabic":"الرسوم الدراسية"},{"word":"dropout","match":"a student who leaves school before finishing","arabic":"منقطع عن الدراسة"},{"word":"critical thinking","match":"the ability to analyze information carefully before you decide","arabic":"التفكير الناقد"},{"word":"plagiarism","match":"copying someone else's work and presenting it as your own","arabic":"السرقة الأدبية / الانتحال"},{"word":"rigorous","match":"very careful, thorough and demanding","arabic":"صارم / دقيق"},{"word":"discipline","match":"a subject or field of study","arabic":"تخصص / مجال معرفي"},{"word":"competence","match":"the ability to do something well","arabic":"كفاءة"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"He is ___ a degree in architecture at King Saud University.","options":["doing up","taking on","making","pursuing"],"answer":"pursuing","explanation":"Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."},{"q":"All assignments must be ___ by Thursday at midnight.","options":["delivered up","given in to","sent off to","submitted"],"answer":"submitted","explanation":"Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."},{"q":"The university awarded her a full ___.","options":["curriculum","dropout","scholarship","tuition"],"answer":"scholarship","explanation":"Education word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"The program helps ___ return to school and finish their education.","options":["scholars","graduates","dropouts","lecturers"],"answer":"dropouts","explanation":"Education word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Medical schools have ___ admission tests.","options":["rigors","rigorous","rigorously","rigor"],"answer":"rigorous","explanation":"Word-family form.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"In academic writing, \"lots of\" should usually be replaced by ___.","options":["tons of","heaps of","plenty","numerous"],"answer":"numerous","explanation":"Formal academic word choice.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة الرسمية."},{"q":"Medicine is one of the most demanding ___ at university.","options":["disciplines","discipline's","disciplined","disciples"],"answer":"disciplines","explanation":"Education word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Students who want to study abroad must first ___ the language requirements.","options":["meet","do","reach up","make"],"answer":"meet","explanation":"Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."},{"q":"Rather than focusing only on academic subjects, the new ______ includes practical courses in coding, financial planning and public speaking.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["dropout","curriculum","plagiarism","tuition"],"answer":"curriculum","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."},{"q":"Because she had copied entire paragraphs from an online article without citing it, the student was found guilty of ______ and had to rewrite her essay.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["literacy","plagiarism","enrollment","competence"],"answer":"plagiarism","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A university orientation day: a large banner \"Welcome to Your Learning Journey\"; booths for \"Scholarships\", \"Vocational Programs\", \"Academic Integrity\" and \"Research Opportunities\"; students holding enrollment forms. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A university orientation day: a large banner \"Welcome to Your Learning Journey\"; booths for \"Scholarships\", \"Vocational Programs\", \"Academic Integrity\" and \"Research Opportunities\"; students holding enrollment forms"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 7 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 7 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows tuition (the money you pay to study, or teaching itself); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing tuition: the money you pay to study, or teaching itself"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows dropout (a student who leaves school before finishing); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing dropout: a student who leaves school before finishing"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows critical thinking (the ability to analyze information carefully before you decide); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing critical thinking: the ability to analyze information carefully before you decide"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows plagiarism (copying someone else's work and presenting it as your own); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing plagiarism: copying someone else's work and presenting it as your own"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows rigorous (very careful, thorough and demanding); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing rigorous: very careful, thorough and demanding"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows discipline (a subject or field of study); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing discipline: a subject or field of study"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-W07","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows competence (the ability to do something well); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing competence: the ability to do something well"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Dominoes”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Dominoes"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-W01","script":"tuition. tuition. Many universities offer free tuition to top students.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-W02","script":"dropout. dropout. The program helps dropouts return to education.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-W03","script":"critical thinking. critical thinking. Critical thinking helps us recognize misinformation.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-W04","script":"plagiarism. plagiarism. Plagiarism is a serious offense at university.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-W05","script":"rigorous. rigorous. Medical schools have rigorous admission tests.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-W06","script":"discipline. discipline. Engineering is a demanding discipline.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-W07","script":"competence. competence. Employers look for competence in communication.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Acquire Knowledge, Think Critically: Education Vocabulary and Academic Collocations”. Let’s learn education vocabulary and academic collocations (acquire knowledge, develop critical thinking, enroll in a program, pursue a degree, submit an assignment, conduct research, meet the requirements, academic performance, rigorous standards, avoid plagiarism); academic word families together. Meet some new words. tuition: the money you pay to study, or teaching itself. dropout: a student who leaves school before finishing. critical thinking: the ability to analyze information carefully before you decide. Academic collocations: acquire / gain knowledge; develop critical thinking / skills; enroll in a course / a program; pursue a degree; major in a subject; attend lectures; submit an assignment; meet a deadline / the requirements; conduct / carry out research; take / sit an exam; improve academic performance; award a scholarship; avoid plagiarism; rigorous standards. Education words: curriculum (all subjects taught), assessment (testing), literacy (reading and writing; or knowledge of a field: digital literacy), vocational (job-skills) education, tuition (fees), dropout (someone who leaves school early), discipline (a field of study), competence (ability), plagiarism (copying others' work). Here are some examples. She enrolled in a vocational program in renewable energy. He is pursuing a degree in computer science. All assignments must be submitted before midnight. Be careful! Some learners say: “I want to make a degree in engineering.” That’s not right. We say: “I want to pursue / earn a degree in engineering.” pursue / earn a degree. Quick check: Is \"research\" countable? … Think! … No – *conduct research*, not \"a research\". Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"enroll in a program\", \"submit an assignment\" and \"conduct research\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.05"}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS4","title":"Among the Challenges Are…: Subject–Verb Agreement in Inverted and Complex Sentences (SAT)","objectives":["Students will be able to make the verb agree with the real subject when the subject comes after the verb.","Students will be able to make verbs agree in long and complex sentences, including relative clauses after \"one of the…\".","I can write \"Among the biggest challenges are time and money.\"","I can write \"She is one of the teachers who use technology every day.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من جعل الفعل يتفق مع الفاعل الحقيقي عندما يأتي الفاعل بعد الفعل.","سيتمكن الطلاب من جعل الأفعال تتفق في الجمل الطويلة والمعقدة، ومنها جمل الوصل بعد one of the…","أستطيع أن أكتب Among the biggest challenges are time and money.","أستطيع أن أكتب She is one of the teachers who use technology every day."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"curriculum","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kɚˈɪkjələm/","definition":"all the subjects and content taught in a school or course","arabic":"المنهج الدراسي","example":"The new curriculum includes coding from Grade 4.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"platform","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈplætˌfɔrm/","definition":"a digital system or website used for a particular purpose","arabic":"منصة","example":"Students submit their homework on an online platform.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"thrive","pos":"verb","ipa":"/θraɪv/","definition":"to grow, develop or be successful","arabic":"يزدهر / ينجح","example":"Some students thrive in online classes.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"lifelong learning","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˈlaɪˈflɔŋ ˈlɝnɪŋ/","definition":"continuing to learn throughout your life","arabic":"التعلّم مدى الحياة","example":"Lifelong learning helps people adapt to new jobs.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"assessment","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈsɛsmənt/","definition":"the process of testing and judging students' learning","arabic":"تقييم","example":"The course has three assessments and a final exam.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"literacy","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlɪtɚəsi/","definition":"the ability to read and write; knowledge of a particular area","arabic":"محو الأمية / المعرفة بمجال","example":"Digital literacy is essential today.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"When the subject comes after the verb, find it before choosing the verb. There is / are: There are many reasons… Among…: Among the biggest challenges are time and money. Inversion: Not only do the students need support…, Rarely does a student… The auxiliary agrees with the subject that follows it.\nIn long subjects, ignore the words between the subject and the verb: The quality of the lessons and the materials is excellent. The number of students who use online platforms has increased. Each of the universities offers scholarships.\nIn one of the + plural noun + who/that, the relative clause usually describes the plural noun, so its verb is plural: She is one of the teachers who use technology every day. But the main verb agrees with one: One of the teachers uses a tablet. Compound subjects: and → plural (Math and physics are…); or / nor → the closer subject (Neither the teacher nor the students were…).\nThere is / are, Among… is / are → look after the verb\ninversion: auxiliary agrees with the subject after it\nlong subjects: find the head noun (The quality of… is)\none of the + plural noun + who + plural verb • One of the… + singular verb","examples":["There are several ways to improve academic performance.","Among the most popular disciplines is computer science.","Not only do the students need laptops, but they also need training.","Rarely does a new curriculum satisfy everyone.","The quality of the courses has improved.","She is one of the professors who encourage critical thinking.","One of the professors encourages critical thinking.","Neither the principal nor the teachers were informed."],"common_errors":["✗ There is many reasons to learn a language. → ✓ There are many reasons to learn a language. (Subject = reasons (plural).)","✗ Among the challenges is time and money. → ✓ Among the challenges are time and money. (Subject = time and money (plural).)","✗ The quality of the lessons are excellent. → ✓ The quality of the lessons is excellent. (Head noun = quality.)","✗ He is one of the students who studies at night. → ✓ He is one of the students who study at night. (who refers to students (plural).)"],"arabic":"عندما يأتي الفاعل بعد الفعل نحدده أولًا: There are many reasons، وAmong the biggest challenges are time and money.\nفي الجمل المقلوبة يتفق الفعل المساعد مع الفاعل الذي يليه: Not only do the students…، Rarely does a student…\nفي الفاعل الطويل نجد الاسم الرئيس: The quality of the lessons is excellent.\nفي one of the students who… يعود who على الجمع فيكون الفعل جمعًا، أما One of the students فالفعل مفرد. وهذه أسئلة شائعة في SAT."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Among the Challenges Are…: Subject–Verb Agreement in Inverted and Complex Sentences (SAT)”. Let’s learn agreement when the subject follows the verb (There is/are…, Among the… is/are…, Here comes…, inverted sentences: Not only do the students…); long subjects with modifiers (The quality of the lessons… is); one of the… who/that + plural verb; each / every; compound subjects (and → plural; or / nor → the closer subject) together.","on_screen":"GV-L10-U1-LS4 | Among the Challenges Are…: Subject–Verb Agreement in Inverted and Complex Sentences (SAT)","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"When the subject comes after the verb, find it before choosing the verb. There is / are: There are many reasons… Among…: Among the biggest challenges are time and money. Inversion: Not only do the students need support…, Rarely does a student… The auxiliary agrees with the subject that follows it.","on_screen":"agreement when the subject follows the verb (There is/are…, Among the… is/are…, Here comes…, inverted sentences: Not only do the students…); long subjects with modifiers (The quality of the lessons… is); one of the… who/that + plural verb; each / every; compound subjects (and → plural; or / nor → the closer subject)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"When the subject comes after the verb, find it before choosing the verb. There is / are: There are many reasons… Among…: Among the biggest challenges are time and money. Inversion: Not only do the students need support…, Rarely does a student… The auxiliary agrees with the subject that follows it. In long subjects, ignore the words between the subject and the verb: The quality of the lessons and the materials is excellent. The number of students who use online platforms has increased. Each of the universities offers scholarships.","on_screen":"There is / are, Among… is / are → look after the verb • inversion: auxiliary agrees with the subject after it • long subjects: find the head noun (The quality of… is)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. There are several ways to improve academic performance. Among the most popular disciplines is computer science. Not only do the students need laptops, but they also need training.","on_screen":"There are several ways to improve academic performance. / Among the most popular disciplines is computer science. / Not only do the students need laptops, but they also need training.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “There is many reasons to learn a language.” That’s not right. We say: “There are many reasons to learn a language.” Subject = reasons (plural).","on_screen":"✗ There is many reasons to learn a language.   ✓ There are many reasons to learn a language.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: \"Among the challenges ___ time and money.\" is or are? … Think! … *are* – the subject is *time and money*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"Among the biggest challenges are time and money.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"Among the biggest challenges are time and money.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: agreement when the subject follows the verb (There is/are…, Among the… is/are…, Here comes…, inverted sentences: Not only do the students…); long subjects with modifiers (The quality of the lessons… is); one of the… who/that + plural verb; each / every; compound subjects (and → plural; or / nor → the closer subject).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","عندما يأتي الفاعل بعد الفعل نحدده أولًا: There are many reasons، وAmong the biggest challenges are time and money.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: There is many reasons to learn a language. — الصحيح: There are many reasons to learn a language.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب Among the biggest challenges are time and money."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Report on Online Learning (editing passage)","body":"There is many advantages to online learning. Among the most important is flexibility and access to experts. The quality of the recorded lessons are generally high. However, one of the problems that concern teachers is cheating during online tests. Students who has good time-management skills tend to do best.","word_count":49,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct verb.","items":[{"q":"There ___ many reasons to learn a second language.","options":["has been","was","is","are"],"answer":"are","explanation":"There is / are.","explanation_ar":"There is / are."},{"q":"Among the biggest challenges ___ time and money.","options":["has","is","are","was"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Agreement after inversion or \"Among…\".","explanation_ar":"الاتفاق بعد القلب."},{"q":"The quality of the lessons and the materials ___ excellent.","options":["are","is","have been","were"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Long subject: find the head noun.","explanation_ar":"الفاعل الطويل."},{"q":"She is one of the teachers who ___ technology every day.","options":["uses","is using","use","has used"],"answer":"use","explanation":"one of the… who / One of the…","explanation_ar":"one of the."},{"q":"Rarely ___ a new curriculum satisfy every teacher.","options":["does","have","is","do"],"answer":"does","explanation":"Agreement after inversion or \"Among…\".","explanation_ar":"الاتفاق بعد القلب."},{"q":"Among the most important skills that employers look for in graduates ______ communication, teamwork and critical thinking.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["has been","is","was","are"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Agreement after inversion or \"Among…\".","explanation_ar":"الاتفاق بعد القلب."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS4-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the correct form of the verb. Word bank: encourages, has, were","items":[{"q":"The number of students who use online platforms ______ (have) increased sharply.","options":[],"answer":"has","explanation":"Long subject: find the head noun.","explanation_ar":"الفاعل الطويل."},{"q":"Neither the principal nor the teachers ______ (be) informed about the change.","options":[],"answer":"were","explanation":"Compound subjects (and / or / nor).","explanation_ar":"الفاعل المركب."},{"q":"One of the professors ______ (encourage) students to ask difficult questions.","options":[],"answer":"encourages","explanation":"one of the… who / One of the…","explanation_ar":"one of the."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"There is several ways to improve your academic performance.","options":[],"answer":"There are several ways to improve your academic performance.","explanation":"is → are. There is / are.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: is → are. There is / are."},{"q":"Not only does the students need laptops, but they also need training.","options":[],"answer":"Not only do the students need laptops, but they also need training.","explanation":"does → do. Agreement after inversion or \"Among…\".","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: does → do. الاتفاق بعد القلب."},{"q":"The results of the national assessment shows a clear improvement.","options":[],"answer":"The results of the national assessment show a clear improvement.","explanation":"shows → show. Long subject: find the head noun.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: shows → show. الفاعل الطويل."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the report.","items":[{"q":"There is many advantages to online learning.","options":[],"answer":"There are many advantages to online learning.","explanation":"is → are. Agreement after inversion or \"Among…\".","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: is → are. الاتفاق بعد القلب."},{"q":"There is many advantages to online learning.","options":[],"answer":"There are many advantages to online learning.","explanation":"is → are. Agreement after inversion or \"Among…\".","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: is → are. الاتفاق بعد القلب."},{"q":"The quality of the recorded lessons are generally high.","options":[],"answer":"The quality of the recorded lessons is generally high.","explanation":"are → is. Agreement after inversion or \"Among…\".","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: are → is. الاتفاق بعد القلب."},{"q":"However, one of the problems that concern teachers is cheating during online tests.","options":[],"answer":"However, one of the problems that concerns teachers is cheating during online tests.","explanation":"concern → concerns. Agreement after inversion or \"Among…\".","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: concern → concerns. الاتفاق بعد القلب."},{"q":"Students who has good time-management skills tend to do best.","options":[],"answer":"Students who have good time-management skills tend to do best.","explanation":"has → have. Agreement after inversion or \"Among…\".","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: has → have. الاتفاق بعد القلب."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write correct sentences.","items":[{"q":"Write a sentence beginning with \"Among the…\" about school subjects.","options":[],"answer":"Among the most useful subjects are math and English.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses agreement when the subject follows the verb (There is/are…, Among the… is/are…, Here comes…, inverted sentences: Not only do the students…); long subjects with modifiers (The quality of the lessons… is); one of the… who/that + plural verb; each / every; compound subjects (and → plural; or / nor → the closer subject) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"one of the… who…\" about a teacher.","options":[],"answer":"Mr. Khalid is one of the teachers who make every lesson interesting.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses agreement when the subject follows the verb (There is/are…, Among the… is/are…, Here comes…, inverted sentences: Not only do the students…); long subjects with modifiers (The quality of the lessons… is); one of the… who/that + plural verb; each / every; compound subjects (and → plural; or / nor → the closer subject) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with a long subject about education.","options":[],"answer":"The number of Saudi students studying abroad has grown in recent decades.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses agreement when the subject follows the verb (There is/are…, Among the… is/are…, Here comes…, inverted sentences: Not only do the students…); long subjects with modifiers (The quality of the lessons… is); one of the… who/that + plural verb; each / every; compound subjects (and → plural; or / nor → the closer subject) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Speed Spell","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a word and a short sentence with it.","Students write the word in 10 seconds.","Show boards on \"Show me!\". Correct = 1 point.","After 10 words, partners check each other's boards and correct any mistakes."],"data":[{"word":"curriculum","clue":"all the subjects and content taught in a school or course"},{"word":"assessment","clue":"the process of testing and judging students' learning"},{"word":"literacy","clue":"the ability to read and write; knowledge of a particular area"},{"word":"vocational","clue":"teaching the skills needed for a particular job"},{"word":"plagiarism","clue":"copying someone else's work and presenting it as your own"},{"word":"competence","clue":"the ability to do something well"},{"word":"platform","clue":"a digital system or website used for a particular purpose"},{"word":"thrive","clue":"to grow, develop or be successful"},{"word":"enroll","clue":"to officially join a school, course or program"},{"word":"tuition","clue":"the money you pay to study, or teaching itself"},{"word":"dropout","clue":"a student who leaves school before finishing"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"There ___ a lot of research on online learning.","options":["are","were","have been","is"],"answer":"is","explanation":"There is / are.","explanation_ar":"There is / are."},{"q":"Among the new courses ___ one on artificial intelligence.","options":["are","is","have been","were"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Agreement after inversion or \"Among…\".","explanation_ar":"الاتفاق بعد القلب."},{"q":"The list of required textbooks ___ on the university website.","options":["is","were","have been","are"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Long subject: find the head noun.","explanation_ar":"الفاعل الطويل."},{"q":"Saad is one of the students who ___ volunteered to tutor younger pupils.","options":["have","is","has","was"],"answer":"have","explanation":"one of the… who / One of the…","explanation_ar":"one of the."},{"q":"Either the students or their teacher ___ going to present the project.","options":["have","were","is","are"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Compound subjects (and / or / nor).","explanation_ar":"الفاعل المركب."},{"q":"","options":["Not only does the program offers free tuition, but it also provides housing.","Not only the program offers free tuition, but it also provides housing.","Not only does the program offer free tuition, but it also provides housing.","Not only do the program offer free tuition, but it also provides housing."],"answer":"Not only does the program offer free tuition, but it also provides housing.","explanation":"Agreement after inversion or \"Among…\".","explanation_ar":"الاتفاق بعد القلب."},{"q":"","options":["Each of the universities have offered scholarships to top students.","Each of the universities offers scholarships to top students.","Each of the universities are offering scholarships to top students.","Each of the universities offer scholarships to top students."],"answer":"Each of the universities offers scholarships to top students.","explanation":"Long subject: find the head noun.","explanation_ar":"الفاعل الطويل."},{"q":"The collection of rare manuscripts that the university library acquired last year ______ now available to researchers from around the world.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["were","is","have been","are"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Long subject: find the head noun.","explanation_ar":"الفاعل الطويل."},{"q":"Dr. Hana is one of the scientists who ______ developed new methods for teaching chemistry through hands-on experiments.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["is","has","was","have"],"answer":"have","explanation":"one of the… who / One of the…","explanation_ar":"one of the."},{"q":"Rarely ______ students in the program fail to complete their degrees, thanks to the strong support offered by their mentors.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["has","does","do","is"],"answer":"do","explanation":"Agreement after inversion or \"Among…\".","explanation_ar":"الاتفاق بعد القلب."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Learning for Tomorrow” that shows agreement when the subject follows the verb (There is/are…, Among the… is/are…, Here comes…, inverted sentences: Not only do the students…); long subjects with modifiers (The quality of the lessons… is); one of the… who/that + plural verb; each / every; compound subjects (and → plural; or / nor → the closer subject) in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Learning for Tomorrow” that shows agreement when the subject follows the verb (There is/are…, Among the… is/are…, Here comes…, inverted sentences: Not only do the students…); long subjects with modifiers (The quality of the lessons… is); one of the… who/that + plural verb; each / every; compound subjects (and → plural; or / nor → the closer subject) in action"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Speed Spell”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Speed Spell"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Among the Challenges Are…: Subject–Verb Agreement in Inverted and Complex Sentences (SAT)”. Let’s learn agreement when the subject follows the verb (There is/are…, Among the… is/are…, Here comes…, inverted sentences: Not only do the students…); long subjects with modifiers (The quality of the lessons… is); one of the… who/that + plural verb; each / every; compound subjects (and → plural; or / nor → the closer subject) together. When the subject comes after the verb, find it before choosing the verb. There is / are: There are many reasons… Among…: Among the biggest challenges are time and money. Inversion: Not only do the students need support…, Rarely does a student… The auxiliary agrees with the subject that follows it. When the subject comes after the verb, find it before choosing the verb. There is / are: There are many reasons… Among…: Among the biggest challenges are time and money. Inversion: Not only do the students need support…, Rarely does a student… The auxiliary agrees with the subject that follows it. In long subjects, ignore the words between the subject and the verb: The quality of the lessons and the materials is excellent. The number of students who use online platforms has increased. Each of the universities offers scholarships. Here are some examples. There are several ways to improve academic performance. Among the most popular disciplines is computer science. Not only do the students need laptops, but they also need training. Be careful! Some learners say: “There is many reasons to learn a language.” That’s not right. We say: “There are many reasons to learn a language.” Subject = reasons (plural). Quick check: \"Among the challenges ___ time and money.\" is or are? … Think! … *are* – the subject is *time and money*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"Among the biggest challenges are time and money.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.05"}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS5","title":"The Classroom of Tomorrow: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to deliver a short formal speech about the future of education.","Students will be able to write a formal speech with inversion, academic vocabulary and correct agreement, and answer SAT-style transition and synthesis items.","I can give a formal speech about learning.","I can use inversion to make my writing more powerful."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من إلقاء كلمة رسمية قصيرة عن مستقبل التعليم.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة كلمة رسمية بالتقديم والتأخير والمفردات الأكاديمية والاتفاق الصحيح، والإجابة عن أسئلة الروابط والتركيب بنمط SAT.","أستطيع أن ألقي كلمة رسمية عن التعلّم.","أستطيع أن أستخدم التقديم والتأخير لجعل كتابتي أقوى."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"curriculum","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kɚˈɪkjələm/","definition":"all the subjects and content taught in a school or course","arabic":"المنهج الدراسي","example":"The new curriculum includes coding from Grade 4.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"platform","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈplætˌfɔrm/","definition":"a digital system or website used for a particular purpose","arabic":"منصة","example":"Students submit their homework on an online platform.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"thrive","pos":"verb","ipa":"/θraɪv/","definition":"to grow, develop or be successful","arabic":"يزدهر / ينجح","example":"Some students thrive in online classes.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"lifelong learning","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˈlaɪˈflɔŋ ˈlɝnɪŋ/","definition":"continuing to learn throughout your life","arabic":"التعلّم مدى الحياة","example":"Lifelong learning helps people adapt to new jobs.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"assessment","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈsɛsmənt/","definition":"the process of testing and judging students' learning","arabic":"تقييم","example":"The course has three assessments and a final exam.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"literacy","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlɪtɚəsi/","definition":"the ability to read and write; knowledge of a particular area","arabic":"محو الأمية / المعرفة بمجال","example":"Digital literacy is essential today.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"vocational","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/voʊˈkeɪʃənəl/","definition":"teaching the skills needed for a particular job","arabic":"مهني","example":"He chose a vocational course in electrical engineering.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"enroll","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɛnˈroʊl/","definition":"to officially join a school, course or program","arabic":"يلتحق / يسجّل","example":"She enrolled in an online programming course.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"tuition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tjuˈɪʃən/","definition":"the money you pay to study, or teaching itself","arabic":"الرسوم الدراسية","example":"Many universities offer free tuition to top students.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"dropout","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdrɑˌpaʊt/","definition":"a student who leaves school before finishing","arabic":"منقطع عن الدراسة","example":"The program helps dropouts return to education.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"critical thinking","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˈkrɪtɪkəl ˈθɪŋkɪŋ/","definition":"the ability to analyze information carefully before you decide","arabic":"التفكير الناقد","example":"Critical thinking helps us recognize misinformation.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"plagiarism","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpleɪdʒɚˌɪzəm/","definition":"copying someone else's work and presenting it as your own","arabic":"السرقة الأدبية / الانتحال","example":"Plagiarism is a serious offense at university.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"rigorous","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈrɪɡɚəs/","definition":"very careful, thorough and demanding","arabic":"صارم / دقيق","example":"Medical schools have rigorous admission tests.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"discipline","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdɪsəplən/","definition":"a subject or field of study","arabic":"تخصص / مجال معرفي","example":"Engineering is a demanding discipline.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"competence","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɑmpətɪns/","definition":"the ability to do something well","arabic":"كفاءة","example":"Employers look for competence in communication.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 1: inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, inversion with only and so/such, academic collocations, and agreement in inverted and complex sentences.\nA formal speech opens with a powerful statement (inversion works well here), develops two or three arguments with evidence, and ends with a memorable message. Use transitions such as however, therefore, moreover and in other words to guide listeners.\n✔ Never have… • Rarely does… • Not only… but also…\n✔ Only when… do… • So + adjective + is/was… that…\n✔ pursue a degree, acquire knowledge, develop critical thinking\n✔ Among the… are… • one of the… who + plural verb","examples":["Never has knowledge been so easy to access.","Rarely do we stop to think about how we learn.","Only by asking questions can we develop critical thinking.","So fast is technology changing that some jobs will disappear.","Among the most valuable skills are curiosity and resilience.","Our teachers are among the people who have shaped our future.","We must acquire new knowledge throughout our lives.","Therefore, lifelong learning is essential."],"common_errors":["✗ Never students have had so many choices. → ✓ Never have students had so many choices. (Inversion.)","✗ Only when we reflect we understand. → ✓ Only when we reflect do we understand. (Invert the main clause.)","✗ Among the skills is critical thinking and teamwork. → ✓ Among the skills are critical thinking and teamwork. (Plural subject.)"],"arabic":"نراجع التقديم والتأخير بعد الظروف المنفية والمقيِّدة ومع only وso/such، والمتلازمات الأكاديمية، والاتفاق في الجمل المعقدة.\nالكلمة الرسمية تبدأ بعبارة قوية (والتقديم مناسب هنا)، وتعرض حججًا بأدلة، وتنتهي برسالة لا تُنسى.\nالروابط مثل however وtherefore وmoreover وin other words ترشد المستمعين."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Classroom of Tomorrow: Language in Use”. Let’s learn inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, so/such inversion, academic collocations, agreement in complex sentences; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L10-U1-LS5 | The Classroom of Tomorrow: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Speeches for tomorrow: in groups, prepare a 90-second speech for Graduation Day about the skills students will need. Include two inversions (Never…, Only when…, Not only…), one so/such inversion, three academic collocations and one sentence with \"Among the… are…\". Deliver the speech; the audience notes each inversion.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 1: inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, inversion with only and so/such, academic collocations, and agreement in inverted and complex sentences. A formal speech opens with a powerful statement (inversion works well here), develops two or three arguments with evidence, and ends with a memorable message. Use transitions such as however, therefore, moreover and in other words to guide listeners.","on_screen":"✔ Never have… • Rarely does… • Not only… but also… • ✔ Only when… do… • So + adjective + is/was… that… • ✔ pursue a degree, acquire knowledge, develop critical thinking","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Never has knowledge been so easy to access. Rarely do we stop to think about how we learn. Only by asking questions can we develop critical thinking.","on_screen":"Never has knowledge been so easy to access. / Rarely do we stop to think about how we learn. / Only by asking questions can we develop critical thinking.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Never students have had so many choices.” That’s not right. We say: “Never have students had so many choices.” Inversion.","on_screen":"✗ Never students have had so many choices.   ✓ Never have students had so many choices.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “Only when we reflect we understand.”? … Think! … It should be “Only when we reflect do we understand.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can give a formal speech about learning.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can give a formal speech about learning.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, so/such inversion, academic collocations, agreement in complex sentences; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع التقديم والتأخير بعد الظروف المنفية والمقيِّدة ومع only وso/such، والمتلازمات الأكاديمية، والاتفاق في الجمل المعقدة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Never students have had so many choices. — الصحيح: Never have students had so many choices.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن ألقي كلمة رسمية عن التعلّم."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"The Classroom of Tomorrow – Sara","body":"Never have students had so many ways to learn as they do today.\nNot only can we watch lessons from the world's best universities, but we can also practice with intelligent apps.\nHowever, rarely does technology alone make someone a better learner.\nOnly when we ask questions, make mistakes and reflect do we truly understand.\nAmong the skills we will need most are critical thinking and teamwork.\nSo quickly is the world changing that no curriculum can teach us everything we will need.\nThat is why lifelong learning is not a luxury; it is a necessity.","word_count":96,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Sara's speech. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Sara thinks students today have fewer ways to learn than in the past.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Classroom of Tomorrow – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"According to Sara, students can watch lessons from the world's best universities.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Classroom of Tomorrow – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Sara believes technology alone usually makes people better learners.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Classroom of Tomorrow – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"She says we understand when we ask questions, make mistakes and reflect.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Classroom of Tomorrow – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Sara mentions critical thinking and teamwork as important skills.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Classroom of Tomorrow – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Sara thinks lifelong learning is a luxury.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Classroom of Tomorrow – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Never ___ so many ways to learn.","options":["students have had","have students had","had students","students had"],"answer":"have students had","explanation":"Inversion for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"التقديم والتأخير."},{"q":"Rarely ___ technology alone make someone a better learner.","options":["does","has","is","do"],"answer":"does","explanation":"Inversion for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"التقديم والتأخير."},{"q":"Among the skills we will need most ___ critical thinking and teamwork.","options":["are","has","is","was"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Subject–verb agreement.","explanation_ar":"الاتفاق."},{"q":"Students who want to succeed must ___ critical thinking.","options":["make","take","develop","do"],"answer":"develop","explanation":"Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."},{"q":"So quickly ___ that no curriculum can teach us everything.","options":["the world changes","the world is changing","does the world changing","is the world changing"],"answer":"is the world changing","explanation":"Inversion for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"التقديم والتأخير."},{"q":"Online lessons give students access to excellent teachers. ______ technology alone cannot make someone a better learner.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Therefore,","Similarly,","For example,","However,"],"answer":"However,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Prepare your speech.","items":[{"q":"A powerful opening with inversion: ___","options":[],"answer":"Never has the world needed curious minds more than it does today.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, so/such inversion, academic collocations, agreement in complex sentences; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A sentence with \"Only when / Only by…\": ___","options":[],"answer":"Only by working together can we solve the problems of tomorrow.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, so/such inversion, academic collocations, agreement in complex sentences; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A sentence with \"So… that\" or \"Such… that\": ___","options":[],"answer":"Such is the speed of change that we must keep learning all our lives.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, so/such inversion, academic collocations, agreement in complex sentences; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A sentence with \"Among the… are…\": ___","options":[],"answer":"Among the most important skills are creativity and communication.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, so/such inversion, academic collocations, agreement in complex sentences; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A memorable closing sentence: ___","options":[],"answer":"Let us never stop learning.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, so/such inversion, academic collocations, agreement in complex sentences; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your speech.","items":[{"q":"Plan: opening, two arguments, evidence, closing message.","options":[],"answer":"Never have we had such opportunities; argument 1: technology; argument 2: skills like critical thinking; evidence: jobs are changing; closing: lifelong learning","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, so/such inversion, academic collocations, agreement in complex sentences; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your speech in 8–9 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Never in history have young people had such opportunities to learn. Not only can we enroll in online courses from top universities, but we can also connect with experts around the world. However, rarely does information alone create wisdom. Only by developing critical thinking can we decide what is true and what is false. Among the skills employers value most are creativity, teamwork and communication. So rapidly is the job market changing that many of tomorrow's jobs do not yet exist. Therefore, each of us has a responsibility to keep learning. Let us leave this school not with the end of our education, but with the beginning of lifelong learning.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, so/such inversion, academic collocations, agreement in complex sentences; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: inversions correct? only-clause in normal order? agreement after \"Among\"? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"Among the skills employers value most is creativity, teamwork and communication\" to \"are creativity, teamwork and communication\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, so/such inversion, academic collocations, agreement in complex sentences; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin the Review Wheel","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["A player spins the wheel and lands on a word.","Say what the word means and use it in a sentence with inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, so/such inversion, academic collocations, agreement in complex sentences; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review).","Teammates check: meaning (1 point), grammar (1 point), pronunciation (1 point).","Highest total after 6 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"curriculum","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"platform","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"thrive","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"lifelong learning","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"assessment","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"literacy","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"vocational","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"enroll","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"tuition","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"dropout","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"critical thinking","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"plagiarism","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"rigorous","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"discipline","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"competence","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Seldom ___ such an inspiring graduation speech.","options":["heard I","I heard","I have heard","have I heard"],"answer":"have I heard","explanation":"Inversion for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"التقديم والتأخير."},{"q":"Only by asking questions ___ develop critical thinking.","options":["students can","students could","can students to","can students"],"answer":"can students","explanation":"Inversion for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"التقديم والتأخير."},{"q":"She hopes to ___ a degree in data science.","options":["take on","pursue","do","make"],"answer":"pursue","explanation":"Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."},{"q":"There ___ several ways to improve your academic performance.","options":["has been","is","are","was"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Subject–verb agreement.","explanation_ar":"الاتفاق."},{"q":"","options":["Not only won she the scholarship, but she also gave the graduation speech.","Not only did she win the scholarship, but she also gave the graduation speech.","Not only she won the scholarship, but she also gave the graduation speech.","Not only did she won the scholarship, but she also gave the graduation speech."],"answer":"Not only did she win the scholarship, but she also gave the graduation speech.","explanation":"Inversion for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"التقديم والتأخير."},{"q":"Many people believe that online learning is easier than classroom learning. ______ it often requires more self-discipline, because no one is there to check on students.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["In fact,","For this reason,","Therefore,","Similarly,"],"answer":"In fact,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"Vocational programs train students for specific careers. ______ graduates often find jobs more quickly than students with general degrees.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["As a result,","In contrast,","However,","Nevertheless,"],"answer":"As a result,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Madrasati is a national online learning platform in Saudi Arabia.\n• It was launched in 2020.\n• Millions of students used it during school closures.\n• Many teachers still use it to set and collect homework.\n\nThe student wants to show that Madrasati has had a lasting effect. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Madrasati was launched in 2020.","Launched during the school closures of 2020, Madrasati is still used by many teachers to set and collect homework.","Madrasati is a national online platform.","Millions of students used Madrasati."],"answer":"Launched during the school closures of 2020, Madrasati is still used by many teachers to set and collect homework.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Lifelong learning means continuing to learn throughout life.\n• Technology is changing many jobs.\n• Some skills become outdated within a few years.\n• Workers who keep learning adapt more easily.\n\nThe student wants to explain why lifelong learning is important. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Because technology is changing jobs so quickly that some skills become outdated within years, workers who keep learning adapt more easily.","Some workers learn new skills.","Lifelong learning means continuing to learn throughout life.","Technology is changing many things."],"answer":"Because technology is changing jobs so quickly that some skills become outdated within years, workers who keep learning adapt more easily.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"Pick the best opening sentence for a formal graduation speech:","options":["Never are we been so ready to face the future.","Never had we been so ready to face the future yesterday.","Never have we been so ready to face the future.","Never we have been so ready to face the future."],"answer":"Never have we been so ready to face the future.","explanation":"Inversion for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"التقديم والتأخير."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"A school auditorium on Graduation Day: Sara at a podium giving a speech; behind her, a screen with \"The Classroom of Tomorrow\"; parents and teachers listening. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A school auditorium on Graduation Day: Sara at a podium giving a speech; behind her, a screen with \"The Classroom of Tomorrow\"; parents and teachers listening"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Learning for Tomorrow”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Learning for Tomorrow”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L10-U1-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin the Review Wheel”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin the Review Wheel"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS5-T1","script":"Never have students had so many ways to learn as they do today. Not only can we watch lessons from the world's best universities, but we can also practice with intelligent apps. However, rarely does technology alone make someone a better learner. Only when we ask questions, make mistakes and reflect do we truly understand. Among the skills we will need most are critical thinking and teamwork. So quickly is the world changing that no curriculum can teach us everything we will need. That is why lifelong learning is not a luxury; it is a necessity.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L10-U1-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Classroom of Tomorrow: Language in Use”. Let’s learn inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, so/such inversion, academic collocations, agreement in complex sentences; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Speeches for tomorrow: in groups, prepare a 90-second speech for Graduation Day about the skills students will need. Include two inversions (Never…, Only when…, Not only…), one so/such inversion, three academic collocations and one sentence with \"Among the… are…\". Deliver the speech; the audience notes each inversion. Today you use all of Unit 1: inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials, inversion with only and so/such, academic collocations, and agreement in inverted and complex sentences. A formal speech opens with a powerful statement (inversion works well here), develops two or three arguments with evidence, and ends with a memorable message. Use transitions such as however, therefore, moreover and in other words to guide listeners. Here are some examples. Never has knowledge been so easy to access. Rarely do we stop to think about how we learn. Only by asking questions can we develop critical thinking. Be careful! Some learners say: “Never students have had so many choices.” That’s not right. We say: “Never have students had so many choices.” Inversion. Quick check: what is wrong with “Only when we reflect we understand.”? … Think! … It should be “Only when we reflect do we understand.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can give a formal speech about learning.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.05"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"Never before ___ so many students study online.","options":["have","was","had","did"],"answer":"had","explanation":"Never / Rarely / Seldom + auxiliary + subject.","explanation_ar":"Never have I."},{"q":"Rarely ___ the professor cancel a lecture.","options":["is","does","do","has"],"answer":"does","explanation":"Add do / does / did when there is no auxiliary.","explanation_ar":"إضافة do / did."},{"q":"Not only ___ the course, but he also helped his classmates.","options":["he did pass","he passed","passed he","did he pass"],"answer":"did he pass","explanation":"Not only + auxiliary + subject…, but also…","explanation_ar":"Not only… but also."},{"q":"Hardly had we sat down ___ the exam began.","options":["than","when","then","that"],"answer":"when","explanation":"Hardly… when / No sooner… than.","explanation_ar":"Hardly… when."},{"q":"No sooner had she submitted the essay ___ she noticed a mistake.","options":["than","when","then","that"],"answer":"than","explanation":"Hardly… when / No sooner… than.","explanation_ar":"Hardly… when."},{"q":"Under no circumstances ______ students allowed to bring phones into the examination hall.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["are","it is","they are","is"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Under no circumstances / At no time / Nowhere + auxiliary + subject.","explanation_ar":"Under no circumstances."},{"q":"Little ___ that his science project would win a national prize.","options":["he did know","knew he","he knew","did he know"],"answer":"did he know","explanation":"Little + did + subject + know / realize.","explanation_ar":"Little did he know."},{"q":"Only when the results were published ___ celebrate.","options":["the students","did the students","the students did","did the students to"],"answer":"did the students","explanation":"Only when / after / if + main-clause inversion.","explanation_ar":"Only when."},{"q":"Only by reading widely ___ a rich vocabulary.","options":["can you build","build you can","you can build","you build"],"answer":"can you build","explanation":"Only by / Only then + inversion.","explanation_ar":"Only by."},{"q":"Not until the last day ___ to revise.","options":["did he start","he did start","he started","started he"],"answer":"did he start","explanation":"Not until + main-clause inversion.","explanation_ar":"Not until."},{"q":"So rigorous ___ that only half the students passed.","options":["the exam did","the exam was","was the exam","did the exam"],"answer":"was the exam","explanation":"So + adjective/adverb + inversion + that.","explanation_ar":"So… that."},{"q":"___ was the success of the reading program that it was expanded nationwide.","options":["Such","So","So much","Such a"],"answer":"Such","explanation":"Such + be + noun + that.","explanation_ar":"Such… that."},{"q":"She is ___ a degree in chemistry.","options":["making","taking on","doing","pursuing"],"answer":"pursuing","explanation":"Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."},{"q":"The students ___ research on air quality near their school.","options":["took","made","conducted","did a"],"answer":"conducted","explanation":"Academic collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الأكاديمية."},{"q":"Many universities use software that can detect copied text, which has made ______ much easier to identify than it was in the past.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["enrollment","plagiarism","literacy","competence"],"answer":"plagiarism","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."},{"q":"There ___ several scholarships available for international students.","options":["was","are","is","has been"],"answer":"are","explanation":"There is / are.","explanation_ar":"There is / are."},{"q":"Among the most popular majors ___ computer science.","options":["have been","were","is","are"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Agreement after inversion or \"Among…\".","explanation_ar":"الاتفاق بعد القلب."},{"q":"The quality of the courses ___ improved dramatically.","options":["are","have","were","has"],"answer":"has","explanation":"Long subject: find the head noun.","explanation_ar":"الفاعل الطويل."},{"q":"Dr. Saad is one of the professors who ___ students to think critically.","options":["encourage","is encouraging","has encouraged","encourages"],"answer":"encourage","explanation":"one of the… who / One of the…","explanation_ar":"one of the."},{"q":"Seldom ______ a single teacher have such a lasting influence on so many students as Mr. Khalid did during his forty-year career.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["is","has","does","do"],"answer":"does","explanation":"Agreement after inversion or \"Among…\".","explanation_ar":"الاتفاق بعد القلب."},{"q":"Online courses allow students to learn at their own pace. ______ they can be difficult for students who struggle with self-discipline.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Similarly,","Therefore,","For example,","However,"],"answer":"However,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Critical thinking is the ability to analyze information carefully.\n• Employers rank it among the most important skills.\n• It helps people recognize misinformation.\n• Many schools now teach it explicitly.\n\nThe student wants to explain why schools teach critical thinking. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Employers rank many skills.","Schools teach many subjects.","Critical thinking is the ability to analyze information.","Because critical thinking helps people recognize misinformation and is highly valued by employers, many schools now teach it explicitly."],"answer":"Because critical thinking helps people recognize misinformation and is highly valued by employers, many schools now teach it explicitly.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"rarely the students has enjoyed such a rigorous course.\"","options":["Rarely has the students enjoyed such a rigorous course.","rarely have the students enjoyed such a rigorous course.","Rarely have the students enjoyed such a rigorous course.","Rarely the students have enjoyed such a rigorous course."],"answer":"Rarely have the students enjoyed such a rigorous course.","explanation":"Add do / does / did when there is no auxiliary.","explanation_ar":"إضافة do / did."},{"q":"\"Only when students feel safe do they ask questions.\" Which clause is inverted?","options":["Neither clause is inverted.","do they ask questions","Only when students feel safe","students feel safe"],"answer":"do they ask questions","explanation":"Normal order in the only/until clause; invert the main clause.","explanation_ar":"قلب الجملة الرئيسة فقط."}],"theme_ar":"التعلّم من أجل الغد","essential_question_ar":"ماذا يحتاج الطلاب أن يتعلّموا لينجحوا في عالم متغيّر؟","can_do":"I can use inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials (Never have I…, Only when…), use so/such inversion for emphasis, discuss education with academic collocations, and make verbs agree in inverted and complex sentences.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أستخدم التقديم والتأخير بعد الظروف المنفية والمقيِّدة (Never have I… / Only when…)، والتقديم مع so/such للتوكيد، وأناقش التعليم بمتلازمات أكاديمية، وأجعل الفعل يتفق مع الفاعل في الجمل المقلوبة والمعقدة."});
